(Children and School Air Quality Safety Guidelines) Tj T*

(Document ID: REF-CHI-2024) Tj T*
(Source: Pediatric Health Association & School Safety Board) Tj T*
(Topic: Protecting Infants, Children, and Students from Air Pollution) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Pediatric Risk Factors:) Tj T*
(1. Higher Respiratory Rate: Children breathe 50% more air per pound of body weight than adults.) Tj T*
(2. Developing Lungs: Inhaled particulates impair pulmonary alveolar development.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(School Recess Guidelines:) Tj T*
(- AQI 0-50: Full outdoor recess and sports allowed.) Tj T*
(- AQI 51-100: Normal outdoor activity; observe asthmatic children closely.) Tj T*
(- AQI 101-150: Limit prolonged outdoor exertion to 15 minutes; asthmatic children stay indoors.) Tj T*
(- AQI 151-200: Move all recess, PE classes, and after-school sports indoors.) Tj T*
(- AQI > 200: Full outdoor activity cancellation; activate classroom HEPA purifiers.) Tj T*
